Summary: recommended only for tycoon passionates, not for everyone. My rate: 6.75/10.
PROS:
- It's basically Prison Architect with airports;
- PERFECT management granularity (not too fine, not too thick: devs really did an excellent job on this);
CONS:
- There is no tutorial (seriously??);
- Not enough feeling of progress nor contents leads the game to be potentially boring after a while (in my case, 30+ hours, which is sufficient);
FURTHER RECOMMENDATIONS:
- The "Fixed" pricing model for fuel is (imo) too easily exploitable to get massive gains. Seriously, it I set up a "Market" pricing model that has +20% surcharge of the current market price, I get almost no airplane willing to refuel. If I set up a "Fixed" pricing model with $2.0 per litre (and I buy massive amounts of fuel when the price drops behind $1.0 per litre) I get a +100% surcharge and I have almost 1/5 of airplaines asking for refuel. This is nonsense.

