Verry dissappointed not by the game, but by the ones who decided to continue to develop the game from the first team. I never seen so much silence from a gaming company about a game and I can`t understand why they didn`t say anything since 2016. No updates, no maintenance, NOTHING! They should be ashamed of that! They should be ashamed for asking people for money in the Early Acess stage when they knew they would drop off the game! This game had so much potential! So much potential that was wasted because of a greedy company!!!
I was a Closed Beta Tester and I`ve noticed a downgrade when it comes to the gameplay of this MMORPG.
The character customization is really basic: gender, body colour and shape of the energy on your body. No other sliders for body or face. There`s 4 classes with 2 roles each: Warrior (Damage/Tank), Assassin (Damage/Tank, Ranged Marksman (Damage/Healer) and Energizer (Damage/Healer).
The class selection screen looks like a browser MMO one. You are just presented with a picture of that class and a brief description of it. Before you can lock on your class you have the possibility to test it in a small tutorial area.
Each class have 3 weapons and somewhere like 7 skills, some of them are unlocked at different levels.
After the tutorial, which takes quite a long time (1-2 hours) you will enter the main area of the game Lambda Mall, which from where you can go to different areas of game.
The combat is pretty basic and there isn`t too much to it. Enemies are quite strong even in the tutorial area so you can only kill one at time.
Overall I don`t recommend this game. It has plenty ammount of bugs, that shouldn`t be there at the time game was released. Personally I stopped playing the game after "PLAY" button stopped working for me. Also, there aren`t many people who play the game. I didn`t met anyone while I was playing and Steam Charts say that overall there is just 1 person per day who play it.
Again, the game had so much pottential that for some reason or another it was wasted right at the start of the game.
I really hope some other company would take it from Drago or at least make the game a single player offline experience.
UPDATE (02.09.2017)
Seems that according to Drago this whole mess was actually because of the investors. Didn`t understood exactly how but they are probably right.
And it sems now that devs (Drago Entertainment) have the full control over the game.
I guess that`s pretty cool since now they can actually work uninterrupted on the game and on it`s bugs.
They also updated the game recently and fixed and added a lot of things.
Among the bugs they fixed and things added is worth mentioning:
* servers are up all the time (except maintenance times);
* fixed the "Play" button not working;
* fixed damage received;
* fixed enemies attacking you while talking with a friendly NPC;
* fixed spawning in the same place where enemies would atack you and kill you again;
* fixed a bug that wouldn`t let you progress past lvl 17;
* added more skins to the character making screen;
* added tatooes and make-up;
* added hairstyles and colours;
* Lambda Mall map is reworked at some parts;
* added a skill purchasing ATM insted of an NPC;
* added an NPC from where you can choose a different skin if you have a ticket;
And probably a lot of other things I can`t remember. I might update this list if I find that to be necessary.
But there are still a lot of things to be changed.
For example, they need to completley overhaul the class selection screen. It still looks like one of those browsers MMORPGs. Also one thing they didn`t fixed is the FPS and PING.
Despite me playing on EU, I still have high PING sometimes. And the FPS is extremely low and not constant no matter what settings you use. You are also very limited at your video settings.
I`m quite happy that tehy didn`t let game to actually die and they are working hard on it.
But at current stage, game is still lightyears compared with the current MMORPGs we have on the market. Drago must work harder if they want to effectively compete with other MMORPS.

NADI Project is a short-story game with no death possible. A playable, first-person adventure with a sad (
) end. Graphics have some glitches, maybe alpha-blending is missing on the corner of the fences near Anna's tomb but the rest is fine. Frame-rate drops in lighthouse tower. The antagonist is silent through the entire game (which is neutral for the voting).
After all 6/10, good music (for a F2P game that costs you zero money) and sounds. If the glitches will be ruled out, 9/10 for sure.

